MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Buc_m01_001: The risks in using Obsidian to summon Demonic\nBeasts are too great.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Buc_m01_002: That Phantom... It is far removed from the laws of\nthis world.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Buc_m01_003: Even if you can control the beasts effectively, I fear\nwhat it will cost you.
MID_LGA_1LED_c06_Buc_m01: <BLN>The risks are too great.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Sci_m01_001: We'll want to pay careful attention to what\nAlexandra, our next opponent, might do.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Sci_m01_002: The Silver Knights of Tellus, from Jurah's temple,\nwere at one point known for their superior skill.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Sci_m01_003: But too many of her matches have been won\nby default.
MID_LGA_1LED_c06_Sci_m01: <BLN>It's rather concerning.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Moo_m01_001: Guess what? I ran into my mom. She was here\nin Dagsion.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Moo_m01_002: <NCA>Say that's good.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Moo_m01_003: <NCB>Ask why she's not more thrilled.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Moo_m01_004: <ACA>Yeah. She seemed alright, but we kinda got into\nan argument...
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Moo_m01_005: <ACB>Because she doesn't listen to a word I say!
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Moo_m01_006: Whatever—it doesn't matter. I'm sticking with\nyou, Leda!
MID_LGA_1LED_c06_Moo_m01: <BLN>I don't even care!
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Oly_m01_001: I happened to run into Alexandra while I was taking\na walk through town.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Oly_m01_002: She seemed to be a perfectly ordinary, honest young\nwoman with nothing to hide.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Oly_m01_003: I know Syracusio has his doubts, but he has his\ndoubts about everything.
MID_LGA_1LED_c06_Oly_m01: <BLN>He's too distrustful.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Car_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Car_m01_001: I am reminded of why I so hated this town.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Car_m01_002: The city was built by command of Dagda the\nGreat, father of the pantheon's gods.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Car_m01_003: I hated being here and feeling the unbearable weight\nof his presence.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Car_m01_004: Your late father, Leilidahna. Did you love him?
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Car_m01_005: I see... In truth, I envy you a little.
MID_LGV_1LED_c06_Car_m01_006: Though of course it is a terrible shame what\nhappened to Guillermo...
MID_LGA_1LED_c06_Car_m01: <BLN>I remember now.